<DocsLayout title="About Octlitch">
    <h1>Octlitch Handbook</h1>

    <p class="docs-lead">
        This is the official documentation for installing, configuring and using
        Octlitch Linux.
    </p>

    <h2>About Octlitch</h2>

    <p>
        Octlitch is a Fedora-based Linux distribution built around KDE Plasma.
        It's primary focus was provide a desktop environment with ass little applications
        as possible while keeping the underlying Linux system accessible.
    </p>

    <p>
        Octlitch uses Fedora packages for the base operating system and DNF
        for system package management.
    </p>

    <p>
        Desktop applications can also be installed through Flatpak and
        Flathub using KDE Discover.
    </p>

    <h2>This handbook</h2>

    <p>
        The handbook covers installation, package management, hardware,
        gaming and troubleshooting.
    </p>

    <p>
        Commands shown in this handbook can be copied directly into a
        terminal unless stated otherwise.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-note">
        <strong>Development release</strong>

        <p>
            Octlitch 1.0 Alpha 1 is still under active development.
            Documentation may change as the distribution evolves.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="docs-next">
        <a href="/documentation/installation/requirements/">
            Next: System requirements →
        </a>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
